## Pinia Store (Setup Store)

```typescript
// stores/useUserStore.ts
export const useUserStore = defineStore('user', () => {
  const users = ref<User[]>([]);
  const isLoading = ref(false);

  function getUserById(id: number) {
    return users.value.find(u => u.id === id);
  }

  return { users, isLoading, getUserById };
});
```

- Use **Setup Store** (function syntax), not Options Store
- Store name = domain: `defineStore('user', ...)`, `defineStore('cart', ...)`

---

## Naming Convention

| Type | Convention | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Component | PascalCase | `UserCard.vue`, `AppButton.vue` |
| Composable | `use` + PascalCase | `useAuth.ts`, `usePagination.ts` |
| Store | `use` + Domain + `Store` | `useUserStore.ts` |
| Route name | camelCase | `userProfile`, `productDetail` |
| Emits | camelCase | `update:modelValue`, `itemSelected` |
